## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] The chapter creates the planned state change.
- [ ] Character knowledge, POV, timeline, objects, injuries, and relationships remain consistent.
- [ ] Required threads move without premature payoff of forbidden threads.
- [ ] The chapter delivers present reader value and records any new reward/hook obligation.
- [ ] Reward family, hook family, emotion curve, opening, and ending do not mechanically repeat the recent rolling window.
- [ ] Always-on style rules and selected scene modes are observable without mechanical repetition.
- [ ] Natural-prose diagnostics find no unresolved generic or synthetic pattern.
- [ ] No source identity, language, setting, character, or plot sequence leaks into the chapter.
